        explanation: "Multiplication is just FAST ADDITION! Instead of adding the same number again and again, we multiply.\n\n3 + 3 + 3 + 3 = 12 → Same as 3 × 4 = 12!\n\nThink of it as GROUPS:\n🍎🍎🍎 🍎🍎🍎 🍎🍎🍎 🍎🍎🍎 = 4 groups of 3 = 12 apples!\n\nParts of multiplication:\n• FACTORS — the numbers you multiply (3 and 4)\n• PRODUCT — the answer you get (12)\n3 × 4 = 12\nfactor × factor = product\n\nImportant rules:\n1. Any number × 1 = the same number (5 × 1 = 5)\n2. Any number × 0 = 0 (5 × 0 = 0, always!)\n3. Order doesn't matter: 3 × 4 = 4 × 3 = 12\n4. Multiplication is repeated addition\n\nWhy learn multiplication?\nBecause addition takes too long for big numbers!\n7 + 7 + 7 + 7 + 7 + 7 + 7 + 7 = ?\nOr just: 7 × 8 = 56! So much faster! ⚡",
